    "galactose_catabolism": {
      "name": "Galactose Catabolism (ED Entry)",
      "type": "independent",
      "kegg_module": {},
      "notes": "Galactose oxidation to galactonate, then entry into ED via bifunctional gnaD. The galactonate \u2192 KDGal conversion is catalyzed by the same gnaD enzyme that handles gluconate \u2192 KDG. KDGal is then cleaved by kdpgA (which handles both KDPG and KDGal substrates) to pyruvate + glyceraldehyde, feeding into the npED glyceraldehyde oxidation step. This pathway is characteristic of marine and soil organisms that encounter galactose from polysaccharide degradation (agar, carrageenan, pectin).",
